    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/18783": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - School of Nursing",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu . Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0112026 Working Title Assistant Professor - School of Nursing Department Org 344000 - Nursing Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas ( UCA ) is seeking a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (9-month appointment) to join the School of Nursing. This on-campus role is designed for a doctorally prepared ( DNP or PhD) Family Nurse Practitioner who will shape the next generation of nursing professionals. The successful candidate will lead innovative educational programs, conduct scholarly research, and contribute to a supportive, inclusive academic environment. Learn more at: www.uca.edu/nursing Job Duties and Responsibilities This tenure track position focuses on teaching, curriculum development, assessment and evaluation, collaboration and mentorship. The faculty member will facilitate student learning, engage in research and scholarship, focus on continuous professional development and provide institutional, professional and community service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities As a tenure-track faculty, you will translate intricate clinical data into digestible, evidence-based instruction. You will ground your teaching in the current realities of healthcare policy and ethics, ensuring students are equipped to navigate the systemic challenges of modern healthcare. Key Responsibilities: Curriculum Innovation: Design and deliver high-impact programs utilizing active learning and high-fidelity simulations. Mentorship & Leadership: Guide novice nurses and colleagues through the nuances of clinical judgment and professional identity. Interdisciplinary Collaboration: Thrive within academic teams to drive institutional excellence and adapt to evolving accreditation standards. Scholarly Contribution: Advance the profession through reflective practice, original research, and advocacy for healthcare equity. Qualifications & Skills: Clinical Mastery: Advanced knowledge of nursing science and delivery systems. Instructional Excellence: Proven ability to apply educational theory to clinical complexity. Dynamic Communication: Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to lead and inspire. Adaptability: A commitment to lifelong learning and the integration of emerging healthcare technologies. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience The candidate MUST have: 1) Doctoral degree (PhD in Nursing or DNP from a nationally accredited institution. 2) APRN certification and licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner and current unencumbered RN license. 3) Significant clinical experience in nursing practice. 4) Prior experience teaching nursing students at the undergraduate and/or graduate level, with a strong understanding of pedagogical principles and instructional methodologies. Candidates who are ABD or who have 3 or less semesters left to complete the doctoral degree will be considered. Must have all clinical requirements mandated by the clinical agencies used for student clinical experiences. These requirements include: 1) MMR (2 vaccines or a positive titer), 2) Varicella (2 vaccines at least 28 days apart or positive titer), 3) Hepatitis B (2 part series or positive surface antibodies above 10), 4) Tdap (must be received within the last 10 years), 5) Tb (Initial testing: Interferon-gamma release assay ( IGRA ) or a tuberculin skin test ( TST ) for persons without documented prior testing, TB disease or latent TB infection ( LTBI ). Retesting: No annual retest or routine serial testing at any interval after baseline in the absence of a known exposure or ongoing transmission is required), 6) Infuenza vaccine (annually); and 7) current CPR certification BLS from American Health Association. Preferred Education and/or Experience It is PREFERRED that the candidate has: 1) Educational preparation as a nurse educator or experience teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. 2) Experience with learning management systems and/or online teaching at the baccalaureate or higher degree. 3) Experience with simulation teaching at the baccalaureate level or higher. 4) Candidates with current practice experience. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Compact RN license in Arkansas. APRN certification and licensure as a Family Nurse Practitioner. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 08/16/2026 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 03/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Submit a cover letter outlining how you meet the requirements and preferences for the position, curriculum vitae, and names of three references with contact information (loaded under “other documents”) via the university online employment at https://jobs.uca.edu . Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts Other Document License or Certification Other Transcripts Veteran's Documents Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19889": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Nurse (10 month)",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Advanced Practice Nurse (10 month) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Advanced Practice Nurse (10 month) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range $71,000 to $72,800 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1332026 Working Title Advanced Practice Nurse (10 month) Department Org 630000 - Office-Student Health Serv Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary This is a 10-month Advanced Practice Registered Nurse position. The Student Health Clinic provides acute medical care to our students, faculty, and staff. For detailed information about our clinic and the services we offer, visit our website at www.uca.edu/studenthealth. Job Duties and Responsibilities Provide clinical services and treatment for UCA students, faculty, and staff as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse. Work within the approved protocols established for the Student Health Center. Provide high-quality healthcare services including the following: Accessible and available health services, education of and effective communication with those served concerning the diagnosis and treatment of their medical conditions, appropriate preventive measures, and use of the healthcare system, treatment that is consistent with clinical impressions and working diagnosis, continuity of care, appropriate, accurate, and complete medical record entries, adequate and appropriate transfer of information when clients are referred to another healthcare provider. Assess current or potential health hazards and current health status, including analysis of health behavior related to lifestyle and culture. Develop, implement, and evaluate plans of care utilizing sound clinical judgements based on assessment of the physical, psychological, emotional, spiritual, societal, and environmental needs of the clients. Assist individuals to assume responsibility for the prevention of illness and the promotion, maintenance, and restoration of health. Consult, refer, and collaborate with other disciplines involved in the delivery of total client care. Utilize the resources of the University community and the surrounding community. Promote collegial relationships with other clinical staff and providers in the community. Demonstrate evidence of continuing professional growth by involvement in peer review and the review of protocols and procedures; participate in or design and conduct research and continuing education. Attend SHC staff meetings and in-services. Demonstrate awareness of legislative issues relating to nursing practice and healthcare. Participate in community education and other professional activities. Serve as a role model for students. Participate in an appropriate emergency response system in conjunction with UCA Police Department. Participate in an infection control program in conjunction with other appropriate university offices and departments. Develop and assure appropriate follow-up on all referrals. Maintain a positive relationship with the University Physician. Delegate tasks as appropriate to Licensed Practical Nurses, ancillary staff, and Clinical Assistants as allowed by Arkansas Nurse Practice Act. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Clinical/direct care. Leadership and collaborative practice. Improving quality and developing practice. Developing self and others. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Must be licensed as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing in accordance with ACA 17-87-303, and must have prescription privileges in the State of Arkansas. Master of Science in Nursing or Doctorate in Nursing is required. Preferred Education and/or Experience University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 01/16/2027 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications APRN for the State of Arkansas Physical Demands Checklist Sitting, Kneeling, Standing, Walking Physical Exertion Light Work - Exerting up to 20 pounds Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date 12/01/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application License or Certification Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19876": {
      "title": "Part-Time Licensed Practical Nurse or Registered Nurse",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Part-Time Licensed Practical Nurse or Registered Nurse Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Part-Time Licensed Practical Nurse or Registered Nurse Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You may be asked for the names and contact information for work related references. Reference letters will not be requested at this time. Posting Details Title Information Working Title Part-Time Licensed Practical Nurse or Registered Nurse Full-Time/Part-Time Part Time Adjunct/Part Time/GA $ Amount $35.00-$40.00/hour Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number A0792026 Department Name Student Health Center Position Summary The Student Health Center is looking for a part-time Licensed Practical Nurse or Registered Nurse who can be available on weekdays. No weekends or holidays will be required. These are flexible hours to be determined by needs. This position is during the school year only. Job Duties and Responsibilities Responsibilities include direct patient care, taking vital signs, short history, brief exam. Assist with procedures (i.e. repair of lacerations, minor surgical procedures) and Women’s Health. Perform lab waived tests as ordered by Physician or APRN . Draw blood for the lab as indicated. Accurately and legibly document findings on patient record using computerized Electronic Medical Record technology. Other duties include patient education, equipment maintenance, and room stocking and cleaning. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments and assist in resolving student concerns. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions of a public or confidential nature. -Demonstrate follow-up contacts and consultations in a timely manner. Required Education and/or Experience Must be a graduate of an accredited nursing program. No experience necessary. New graduates welcome to apply, we will train. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) License by the Arkansas State Board of Nursing or a compact state. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Background Check Requirements 00 - 01 - Criminal/Sex/Drug Desired start date 01/04/2027 Posting Detail Information Employment is contingent upon the availability of funds and course enrollments Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/03/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants You may be asked for the names and contact information for work related references. Reference letters will not be requested at this time. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you licensed by the State of Arkansas Yes No * Have you ever received State Board of Nursing sanctions in any state? Yes No * Please list the electronic health record systems you have used. (Open Ended Question) * What steps do you take to protect patients’ rights and confidentiality? (Open Ended Question) * How would your boss and co-workers describe you? (Open Ended Question) * Tell me about a challenge or conflict you've faced at work, and how you dealt with it. (Open Ended Question) * What do you consider to be your weaknesses? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application License or Certification Veteran's Documents Other Document Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19845": {
      "title": "Part Time/Hourly College Square Housekeeper",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Part Time/Hourly College Square Housekeeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Part Time/Hourly College Square Housekeeper Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Working Title Part Time/Hourly College Square Housekeeper Full-Time/Part-Time Part Time Adjunct/Part Time/GA $ Amount $15.00 per hour Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Position Details Position Information Posting Number A0752026 Department Name College Square Retirement Ctr Position Summary College Square, the university’s independent living retirement community, is looking for a part-time housekeeper. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. Job Duties and Responsibilities Duties include routine cleaning of apartments and common areas, laundry, maintains and compiles reports and assists with emergencies as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Holidays may be required. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments and assist in resolving student concerns. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions of a public or confidential nature. -Demonstrate follow-up contacts and consultations in a timely manner. Required Education and/or Experience Ability to perform general housekeeping duties. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Must have, or be willing to obtain, CPR and First Aid Certification. Must be detail and multi-task oriented and have strong customer service skills. Must be comfortable working independently. Prior experience in housekeeping/custodial related position as well as working with senior adults preferred. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Background Check Requirements 00 - 01 - Criminal/Sex/Drug Desired start date 11/16/2026 Posting Detail Information Employment is contingent upon the availability of funds and course enrollments Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 10/27/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Veteran's Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
