    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19615": {
      "title": "Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Requesting the following as part of application submittal: -3 Letters of Recommendation Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0372026 Working Title Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Department Org 331000 - Art Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Department of Art and Design at the University of Central Arkansas invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer I position in the Interior Design Program beginning January 2, 2027. The department seeks a candidate whose teaching and professional interests connect historical precedent, preservation research, and contemporary interior design practice. In addition to teaching responsibilities, this position will serve as Curriculum and NCPE Coordinator, supporting the Interior Design Program&#39;s National Council for Preservation Education ( NCPE ) Certificate of Proficiency and assisting with curriculum assessment, course coordination, accreditation support, and continuous improvement initiatives. The successful candidate will support the programs initiatives in historic preservation, sustainability, accreditation, interdisciplinary collaboration, study abroad, and professional preparation. The position will also serve as a strong advocate for the Interior Design Program through collaboration with students, faculty, alumni, advisory board members, professional organizations, and industry partners. This is a nine-month faculty appointment with an expected teaching load of twelve credit hours per semester. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in design history, architectural history, historic preservation, and related subject areas. Teach assigned Art Foundations coursework as needed by the department. Serve as Curriculum and NCPE Coordinator for the Interior Design Program. Maintain student records and documentation associated with the National Council for Preservation Education ( NCPE ) Certificate of Proficiency. Assist with coordination, assessment, and continuous improvement of the preservation curriculum. Work closely with the Program Director to maintain curriculum maps, course sequencing documentation, assessment records, curriculum databases, and course cohesion across the curriculum. This position will serve on the Art & Design Curriculum committee. Support course coordination and curricular cohesion across the Interior Design Program. Participate in curriculum assessment, accreditation documentation, and continuous improvement activities associated with CIDA , NASAD , NCPE , and university requirements. Support study abroad initiatives, experiential learning opportunities, and community-engaged preservation projects. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Participate in recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Serve as a strong advocate for the Interior Design Program and its students. Collaborate with industry partners, alumni, advisory board members, and community stakeholders to advance program initiatives. Participate in departmental, college, university, and program-area meetings and committees. Collaborate with faculty across Interior Design, Studio Art, Art Education, and related disciplines. Maintain active professional engagement and contribute to the advancement of the discipline through professional practice, scholarship, or service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated expertise in architectural history, interiors history, historic preservation, preservation research, or closely related subject matter. Evidence of successful teaching, scholarship, professional practice, or a combination thereof. The successful candidate will contribute to a nationally accredited interior design program through teaching, service, student mentorship, and professional engagement. Primary responsibilities include teaching History of Architecture, Interiors, and Furnishings I; History of Architecture, Interiors, and Furnishings II; Historic Research for Interior Preservation; and selected Art Foundations courses such as 2D Design, 3D Design, Drawing, or Fabrication based on departmental needs and candidate qualifications. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Master’s degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, Historic Preservation, Architectural History, Art History, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. NCIDQ certification or ability to obtain NCIDQ certification within one year of appointment. For Visiting Assistant Professor: Earned doctorate (PhD, DDes, EdD, or equivalent terminal degree) in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, Historic Preservation, Architectural History, Art History, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. NCIDQ certification or ability to obtain NCIDQ certification within one year of appointment. Preferred Education and/or Experience Terminal Degree and NCIDQ Certificate License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) LEED and/or WELL Certification in addition to professional membership in ASID , IIDA , AIA or similar organization University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 01/04/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Requesting the following as part of application submittal: -3 Letters of Recommendation Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Additional Documents Teaching Philosophy License or Certification Veteran's Documents Writing Sample Other Transcripts Other Document Portfolio / Supplemental Materials University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19900": {
      "title": "Benefits Specialist",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Benefits Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Title Information Full-Time/Part-Time Full Time Salary Range Commensurate with experience Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Hybrid Position Details Position Information Posting Number NC1372026 Working Title Benefits Specialist Department Org 501000 - Human Resources Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Benefits Specialist is responsible for analyzing and completing agency/institution human resources program goals and objectives, policies, and procedures. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy Job Duties and Responsibilities This is a fast-paced, high-level role responsible for administering comprehensive health, dental, and vision benefit programs. The Benefits Specialist manages the complete lifecycle of employee benefits enrollment, data auditing, and payroll system integration while delivering exceptional internal customer service. Key Responsibilities Enrollment & Lifecycle Management: Process qualifying life events, approve new hire enrollments, and manage pending tasks and documentation within the Benefitfocus system. Payroll & System Integration: Audit semi-monthly benefits deduction files, perform required overrides, and load accurate data into Banner for seamless payroll processing. Employee Support & Engagement: Serve as the primary point of contact to resolve employee insurance inquiries, and assist in planning open enrollment events and on-campus informational meetings. Reporting & Quality Assurance: Generate semi-monthly and ad hoc reports to ensure data accuracy, maintain comprehensive employee benefit records, and monitor the dedicated benefits email queue daily. Specialized Processing: Administer employee gap claims and coordinate benefits adjustments for internal personnel transfers. Cross-Functional Support: Execute other duties as assigned and serve as the primary backup for both the Leave Specialist and the Offboarding/Retirement Specialist. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The applicant must be very efficient, highly motivated and know how take initiative when it comes to researching, analyzing and finding answers related to benefits, reporting, and other related human resources issues. This includes proficiency in the knowledge of excel. The applicant must possess knowledge of the principles and practices of human resources. Knowledge of state and federal personnel laws, policies, and procedures. Knowledge of payroll and benefits processes. Ability to analyze information and recommend appropriate action. Ability to prepare and present oral and written information and reports. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. -Banner and Benefitfocus Software knowledge is preferable. -Proficient in Excel and Microsoft Office. Required Education and/or Experience The formal educational equivalent of a bachelor’s degree in human resources, public administration, or a related field; plus one year of human resources experience. Additional requirements determined by the agency for recruiting purposes require review and approval by the Office of Personnel Management. OTHER JOB RELATED EDUCATION AND /OR EXPERIENCE MAY BE SUBSTITUTED FOR ALL OR PART OF THESE BASIC REQUIREMENTS , EXCEPT FOR CERTIFICATION OR LICENSURE REQUIREMENTS , UPON APPROVAL OF THE QUALIFICATIONS REVIEW COMMITTEE . Preferred Education and/or Experience Experience working in benefits or a related position, higher education setting, and Ellucian Banner. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 01/04/2027 Position Summary and Qualifications License(s)/Certifications Physical Demands Checklist Sitting Physical Exertion Administrative Work - Exerting up to 10 pounds Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/05/2026 Close Date 11/20/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Veteran's Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19904": {
      "title": "Director of Clinical Education (DCE), Clinical Instructor I",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Director of Clinical Education (DCE), Clinical Instructor I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Director of Clinical Education (DCE), Clinical Instructor I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0422026 Working Title Director of Clinical Education (DCE), Clinical Instructor I Department Org 346000 - Physical Therapy Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Instructor is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is non-tenure track and a twelve-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities The Director of Clinical Education ( DCE ) is a physical therapist whose primary concern is relating the student’s clinical education to the curriculum. The DCE also is responsible for communicating with and educating all Clinical Faculty in matters related to clinical education. The DCE , in association with the academic and clinical faculty coordinates and administers the clinical education process. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge Thorough understanding of CAPTE accreditation standards and DPT curriculum design. Expertise in clinical assessment methodologies, adult learning principles, and tools (e.g., APTA CPI ). Solid grasp of regulatory requirements, clinical education contracts (MOUs), HIPAA , and FERPA compliance. Skills Advanced organizational and administrative management, including experience with clinical tracking software (e.g. CORE Higher Ed). Strong negotiation, conflict resolution, and interpersonal communication skills across diverse stakeholders (students, faculty, site directors). Effective project management for tracking multi-site placements, student performance metrics, and site evaluations. Abilities Ability to build, evaluate, and sustain partnerships with diverse clinical sites and clinical faculty. Ability to mentor, advise, and remediate DPT students in academic and clinical environments. Ability to collaborate with academic faculty to seamlessly integrate didactic coursework with clinical experiences. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Earned academic (PhD, EdD, DSc) or professional ( DPT ) doctoral degree from an accredited institution. Minimum of 3–5 years of clinical PT experience, including documented experience as a Clinical Instructor (CI) or Site Coordinator of Clinical Education ( SCCE ). Preferred Education and/or Experience License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Active, unencumbered Physical Therapist (PT) license in the state of Arkansas. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 05/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 11/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19897": {
      "title": "Academic Dean-College of Health and Behavioral Sciences",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Academic Dean-College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Academic Dean-College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Search Committee invites letters of nomination and applications (letter of interest, full resume/CV, and contact information of at least five references) to be submitted to the search firm assisting the university. References will not be contacted without prior permission of the applicant. Review of materials will begin immediately and continue until the appointment is made. It is preferred, however, that all nominations and applications are submitted before Monday, January 25, 2027. Please submit electronic applications directly to Parker Executive Search. For additional information, please contact: Porsha Williams, Vice President and Managing Director, Higher Education Jacob Anderson, Senior Principal Scott Gaffney, Associate Parker Executive Search Five Concourse Parkway, Suite 2875 | Atlanta, GA 30328 (770) 804-1996 x 111 pwilliams@parkersearch.com | janderson@parkersearch.com | sgaffney@parkersearch.com The search will be conducted in accordance with the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. For additional information about the university and Conway community, please visit the following websites: http://www.uca.edu and http://www.cityofconway.org Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0502026 Working Title Academic Dean-College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Department Org 410000 - Office-Provost Office Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas invites applications and nominations for the position of Dean of the College of Health and Behavioral Sciences ( CHBS ). As UCA’s largest academic college by declared majors and a leading contributor to Arkansas’s healthcare and behavioral health workforce, CHBS offers an exceptional opportunity for an accomplished and entrepreneurial academic leader. Job Duties and Responsibilities Reporting to the Provost and Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs, the dean serves as the college’s chief academic and administrative officer. The dean provides leadership for academic programs, faculty and staff, budgets and resource planning, personnel processes, program quality and assessment, specialized accreditation, clinical operations and partnerships, enrollment and student outcomes, interdisciplinary initiatives, scholarship, advancement, and engagement with the university and broader community. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The position demands excellent communication skills and proven ability to facilitate consensus, evidence of effective academic leadership and administrative experience at the department chair level or above. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience An earned doctorate in a discipline in or closely related to the College, together with a record of teaching, research, and scholarly achievement that merits appointment as a tenured full professor in one of the College’s academic units. Demonstrated academic leadership and progressively responsible administrative experience at the level of department chair, school director, associate dean, dean, or comparable level. Preferred Education and/or Experience Proven ability to manage the budget, personnel, facilities, and other resources of a complex, multi-unit academic organization with fiscal responsibility and transparency. A demonstrated record of success in fundraising and securing external support from donors, alumni, foundations, corporate partners, and public sources, or a genuine and demonstrable commitment to engaging in that work. A commitment to shared governance and to transparent, collaborative decision-making that engages faculty, staff, and students. A record of recruiting, retaining, developing, and mentoring high-quality faculty and staff, and of rewarding excellence in teaching, research, and service. Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to serve as the principal internal and external spokesperson and advocate for the College across multiple constituencies. A demonstrated commitment to student success at every stage of the academic experience, including access, retention, persistence, graduation, and career outcomes. The ability to foster interdisciplinary collaboration within the College and across the university, to build a shared identity and sense of common purpose among different academic units, and to contribute to institutional priorities. The highest standards of personal and professional integrity and ethical conduct. A strong record of research, scholarship, or creative activity, including success in obtaining external funding, and experience advancing a college’s research productivity and impact. In-depth knowledge of clinical and professional programs, including clinical placements, affiliation agreements, specialized program accreditation, and the delivery of community-based services. Experience leading or overseeing clinical operations, such as university-based clinics, community health services, or simulation centers, including attention to quality of care, regulatory compliance, and financial sustainability. Experience building partnerships with healthcare systems, community organizations, government agencies, industry, and nonprofit partners that advance the academic and service missions of the College. Fluency in enrollment management, demographic and workforce trends, and the range of curriculum delivery modes, including online, hybrid, and accelerated formats at the undergraduate and graduate levels, needed to keep programs competitive and relevant while maintaining academic rigor. An entrepreneurial orientation toward enrollment growth, program development, continuing and professional education, and mission-aligned revenue generation that supports the long-term financial health of the College. A record of supporting high-quality teaching, faculty scholarship, student success, and academic or professional program quality. Ability to lead collaboratively across multiple disciplines, build trust, communicate effectively, and manage complex decisions with integrity. Experience leading across multiple campuses, sites, or delivery locations and addressing the needs of stakeholders in each. Working knowledge of faculty personnel processes, including reappointment, promotion, and tenure, and of faculty governance structures. Experience leading organizational change. Comfort using data from multiple sources, including enrollment, workforce, financial, and academic performance data, to inform strategy, program development, resource allocation, and policy. A relational and approachable leadership style characterized by active listening, empathy, humility, and a visible, engaged presence with faculty, staff, and students. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 05/16/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 10/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The Search Committee invites letters of nomination and applications (letter of interest, full resume/CV, and contact information of at least five references) to be submitted to the search firm assisting the university. References will not be contacted without prior permission of the applicant. Review of materials will begin immediately and continue until the appointment is made. It is preferred, however, that all nominations and applications are submitted before Monday, January 25, 2027. Please submit electronic applications directly to Parker Executive Search. For additional information, please contact: Porsha Williams, Vice President and Managing Director, Higher Education Jacob Anderson, Senior Principal Scott Gaffney, Associate Parker Executive Search Five Concourse Parkway, Suite 2875 | Atlanta, GA 30328 (770) 804-1996 × 111 pwilliams@parkersearch.com | janderson@parkersearch.com | sgaffney@parkersearch.com The search will be conducted in accordance with the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. For additional information about the university and Conway community, please visit the following websites: http://www.uca.edu and http://www.cityofconway.org Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
